<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Sept 17.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Sept 17.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF SEPTEMBER 17 VERSUS SEPTEMBER 10, 1996	 DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   11/20    1/0     233/217  105/113  350/350    190</p>
<p> SASK.	3/5   0/0	61/58     8/10    72/73	45</p>
<p> B.C.	 2/2     1/0	18/9     14/21    35/32	14</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/2	2/2	4/4	  0</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 2/3	0/1	2/4	  2</p>
<p> TOTAL     16/27    2/0     316/289  129/147  463/463    251</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS. -- Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624</p>
